      "seed": 1744598599,
      "version": 566,
      "versionNonce": 1214124743,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794409994798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTES",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTES",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TTIgLyo1yt-FTVuFLALKc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1153.6506138208135,
      "y": 904.2456764587937,
      "width": 842.6193237304688,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 524656169,
      "version": 1608,
      "versionNonce": 1824399847,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794409994798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Once on an SM, each block is cut into warps of 32 threads with consecutive \nthread indices.Warps per block = div_ceil(block size, 32).\n\nPadding: a block size not a multiple of 32 leaves its last warp short;\nthe hardware fills it with inactive threads. Happens in EVERY block,\ncomes from MY block-size choice. Always avoidable. Use a multiple of\n32 (128, 256, 512 are the usual picks).\n\nExtras: threads are launched in whole blocks, data comes in any size; div_ceil(n, block)\nrounds the grid UP, so the last block has (blocks x block - n) threads with no data.\n`if i < n` switches them off. Comes from the DATA size, usually unavoidable,\nlast block only.\n\nBoth kinds occupy seats in the pools and cores in every pass while doing nothing.\nPadding is the mistake; extras are the normal cost.\n\nTotal warps = blocks x warps per block: the count the SM's dispatchers work\nthrough, padded and extra threads included.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Once on an SM, each block is cut into warps of 32 threads with consecutive \nthread indices.Warps per block = div_ceil(block size, 32).\n\nPadding: a block size not a multiple of 32 leaves its last warp short;\nthe hardware fills it with inactive threads. Happens in EVERY block,\ncomes from MY block-size choice. Always avoidable. Use a multiple of\n32 (128, 256, 512 are the usual picks).\n\nExtras: threads are launched in whole blocks, data comes in any size; div_ceil(n, block)\nrounds the grid UP, so the last block has (blocks x block - n) threads with no data.\n`if i < n` switches them off. Comes from the DATA size, usually unavoidable,\nlast block only.\n\nBoth kinds occupy seats in the pools and cores in every pass while doing nothing.\nPadding is the mistake; extras are the normal cost.\n\nTotal warps = blocks x warps per block: the count the SM's dispatchers work\nthrough, padded and extra threads included.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "gridSize": 20,
    "gridStep": 5,
    "gridModeEnabled": false,
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff"
  },
